0, Italy +5, Japan flat-to-down), times a semi-elasticity of 2.5 bp per pp (shaded from the Laubach 3-4 bp range, but NOT shaded further because 2A records the convenience yield eroding).\n + AI/grid capex investment demand: +7. Gross arrow is +0.8% of G7 GDP of incremental investment demand x 30 bp per 1% = +24 bp, but probability-weighted by survival of the impulse into 2032-36 at only ~0.30 given AI-Q4 at 66% (my coupled 72%). A bust removes exactly this arrow.\n - precautionary saving (aging plus income insecurity from cognitive-labour compression): -20.\n - saving-propensity effect of cognitive-labour compression (income shifting to capital owners with a higher MPS; the BIS Box C channel seen from the saving side): -10.\n r* net = +32.\n + real term premium: +20 (higher MOVE floor, levered basis-trade absorption replacing price-insensitive official and bank demand, eroded convenience yield).\n + Japan normalization from ~0.40 toward ~0.95 real: +8 on the weighted average.\n - financial-repression wedge: -12 (0.30 probability of explicit YCC / regulatory duration absorption in at least one G7 member x -40 bp).\n - US-specific convergence as the capex impulse fades (US real sits 65 bp above the weighted mean): -15.\n - swap-vs-breakeven resolution fork: -10 expected. The Auditor's point is arithmetically right and nobody else priced it: \"nominal minus TIPS breakeven\" tautologically returns the linker real yield inclusive of a +10 to +25 bp liquidity premium, while \"nominal minus 10y inflation swap\" returns a figure 15-30 bp LOWER (swap-cash basis, CPI floor, indexation lag). The \"/\" is a ~20-40 bp fork — larger than most plausible macro disagreement about the path.\nSUM: 1.95 + 0.32 + 0.20 + 0.08 - 0.12 - 0.15 - 0.10 = 2.18 -> P50 2.15.\nSPREAD: sigma ~0.95, deliberately RIGHT-skewed because the debt-supply arrow is near-certain and monotone while every suppressive arrow is state-contingent. P10 1.05 = regime D (demand shortfall, deflation scare, balance-sh